    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 252159\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n159 PM PST Wed Nov 25 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Breezy north winds along the Colorado River Valley today and \n  Thursday while temperatures rise areawide into the weekend. \n\n* A potentially substantial storm system may impact the first half \n  of next week. \n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...Today through Early Next Week.\n\nGenerally quiet weather through Thanksgiving Weekend. A passing \ndisturbance will temporarily disrupt the ridging pattern today as it \nmoves down the Mexican coast and closes off over the Baja Peninsula. \nA decent north to south pressure gradient will produce sustained \nwinds to around 25 mph in the Colorado River Valley near Laughlin \nalong with waves between 1 and 3 feet on Lake Mohave tonight and \nThanksgiving. Meanwhile, temperatures return to above normal values \nstarting Thursday through the weekend as the disturbance moves out \nand the ridge builds. Afternoon highs will be 5 to 10 degrees above \nnormal for this time of year, or the upper 60s to 70s across the \ndesert valleys. Another weak shortwave will traverse the Great Basin \non Sunday. Besides light snowfall above 7500 feet in the Eastern \nSierra, this will have little impact on weather across the area. \n\nA more potent system looks to bring high elevation snowfall, valley \nrainfall, elevated winds, and cooler temperatures starting early-to-\nmidweek next week. Models continue to slow down on timing, with the \ngreatest precipitation potential now late Tuesday into Wednesday. A \nslight northerly track with the latest run corresponds to a decrease \nin QPF areawide and lower mountain snow totals as moisture gets \nblocked by the Sierra. At the same time, a more northerly track \nwould support a belt of elevated southwesterly winds across the \nMojave Desert. Confidence in forecast details and specific impacts \nremains low at this time given the frequent adjustments in model \noutput. Stay tuned for updates. \n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 00Z Forecast Package...Winds\nwill remain under 8 knots, favoring typical daily directional \ntrends through the TAF period. VFR conditions will persist with \nFEW to BKN high clouds aoa 20 kft will filtering through the area.\n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast\nCalifornia...For the 00Z Forecast Package...With the exception of\nthe lower Colorado River Valley, winds will remain under 10 knots\nand will favor typical daily directional trends through the TAF \nperiod. Elevated northerly winds, gusting 15 to 25 knots, will \ncontinue down the Colorado River Valley through the TAF period. \nFEW to BKN high clouds aoa 20 kft will filtering through the area.\n\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Meltzer\nAVIATION...Stessman\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
